{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Halleluiah.</b> The poet's words, by way of prophecy, praise HaShem when he sees in a vision that HaShem will build Jerusalem and gather the outcasts of Israel." "<b>And the word זמרה</b> — a verb noun, like ליסרה אתכם, and the he is added because it serves on account of what follows: כי טוב זמרה אלהינו כי נעים וכי נאוה — from the root of תאוה, as I explained, that the word is in the nif'al pattern, like וכל נעשה במרחשת."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 147, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:57.618490481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}